ot  declining the vaccine they've had the  first days but they need the second dose  to provide that high level of protection  and similarly  there are 4.4 million of the over 40s  who again  need that second dose and with the delta  variant now making up nine in ten of the  cases across the uk  it's vital we bridge the gap and get  many more people that life-saving second  jab  this extra time will allow us to get  more needles into more arms  getting us the protection we need and  enabling us to see restrictions  fall away on the 19th and in that vein  i would remind colleagues the quote from  the prime minister on monday  where he was very clear that as things  stand and on the basis of the evidence i  can see  right now i'm confident we will not need  any more than four weeks  and that we won't need to go beyond july  the 19th  um turning madame deputy speaker to the  choice we fake  um very very briefly but it needs to be  very brief because i've only got three  minutes  you've just said that the prime minister  has given assurances there's another  four weeks but we've had this time and  time again why should the british people  believe the prime minister now  yeah well the short answer is the  british people do believe the prime  minister  now madame deputy speaker we face a  difficult choice  and my honourable friend the member for  bosworth set it out  extremely clearly it reflects that  underlying debate  about risk we know  and i am clear that we must learn to  live with this disease  and learn to live with it without the  sort of restrictions we have  seen we cannot eradicate it and i have  to say again  rather than relying on the views of the  member for leeds east i'm more inclined  to rely on the views of the member for  north somerset the right honourable  member for north somerset  who made that point very clear and being  very clear those who advocate a zero  covid  must realize that is impractical  unachievable and i consistently  do not subscribe